-- title:
--   Completion of a flat local W-algebra of relative dimension one
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative noetherian local ring that is complete and separated for the adic filtration by its maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_W$, and let $R$ be a commutative noetherian local ring equipped with a $W$-algebra structure whose structure map $W \to R$ is a local homomorphism and makes $R$ flat as a $W$-module. Assume: (i) the composite of $W \to R$ with the residue map $R \to R/\mathfrak m_R$ is surjective, so that $R$ and $W$ have the same residue field; (ii) there is an element $t \in R$ with $\mathfrak m_R = \mathfrak m_W R + (t)$, the sum of the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_W$ and the principal ideal generated by $t$; and (iii) the Krull dimension of the closed fibre $R/\mathfrak m_W R$ equals $1$. Then there exists a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak m_R$-adic completion of $R$ onto the power series ring $W\llbracket X \rrbracket$ such that $e$ carries the image in the completion of $a \in W$ (via $W \to R \to \widehat R$) to the constant series $a$, and carries the image of $t$ to the variable $X$.
--
--   This is the structure theorem identifying the completion of a flat local algebra of relative dimension one over a complete noetherian local ring, with the same residue field, as a power series ring in one variable over the base, the variable being any element cutting out the closed point on the closed fibre. It is the commutative-algebra input to [`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_adicCompletion_stalk_ringEquiv_powerSeries_of_smoothOfRelativeDimension_one`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.exists_adicCompletion_stalk_ringEquiv_powerSeries_of_smoothOfRelativeDimension_one), which computes completed local rings of a smooth relative curve.
